WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.168 --> 00:00:16.973
"Get ready," Teplo croaked hoarsely.

2
00:00:16.974 --> 00:00:24.185
Zann and Perda rubbed their hands together as Teplo let out several loud grunts. "Shift," Perda whispered.

3
00:00:24.186 --> 00:00:30.978
Zann focused on sending Teplo's grunts away so that they seemed to be coming from the guard troll.

4
00:00:30.979 --> 00:00:36.164
The other trolls heard. They turned to look at the guard and noticed the turnip prisoners.

5
00:00:36.165 --> 00:00:40.915
"It's working!" Darb whispered. "They think all their prisoners just escaped!"

6
00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:45.640
The turnip prisoners were still running, luring the trolls away from the pen.

7
00:00:45.641 --> 00:00:53.063
"Go!" Teplo gasped. "Hurry! I'm not sure how much longer I can hold all the illusions steady."

8
00:00:53.064 --> 00:00:56.804
Zann and the others rushed out of their hiding place.

9
00:00:56.805 --> 00:01:02.291
"I'll blast the lock," Fala said. "Get ready to help everyone to the exit."

10
00:01:02.292 --> 00:01:06.016
The prisoners had seen what was happening.

11
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:09.624
As soon as Fala opened the door, they started running out.

12
00:01:09.625 --> 00:01:13.449
Zann and his friends helped them all find the exit through the hedge.

13
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.930
Even Zing helped by hovering over the spot and whistling.

14
00:01:16.931 --> 00:01:23.470
"Gliss!" Perda cried, rushing to grab her friend's hand when she emerged. "This way! Hurry!"

15
00:01:23.471 --> 00:01:29.147
Zann started to follow the girls. Then he heard a weak voice crying out somewhere behind him.

16
00:01:29.148 --> 00:01:34.131
"Help! Please wait for me. Oh dear!"

17
00:01:34.132 --> 00:01:40.337
It was the elderly woman. She was following a stray turnip prisoner that was running toward the trolls.

18
00:01:40.338 --> 00:01:42.686
"Oh no!" Zann murmured.

19
00:01:42.687 --> 00:01:47.591
He raced after the woman. She was already much too close to the trolls.

20
00:01:47.592 --> 00:01:51.242
If he didn't stop her, she'd be recaptured for sure.

21
00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:54.411
And everyone knew that trolls had a bad temper.

22
00:01:54.412 --> 00:01:56.707
Who knew what they'd do to punish her?

23
00:01:56.708 --> 00:02:00.353
"Stop!" Zann grabbed her arm. "Come this way!"

24
00:02:00.354 --> 00:02:09.375
The woman stopped, looking confused. At the same moment, Zann saw one of the trolls turn and spot them. Grunting, it lumbered toward them.

25
00:02:09.376 --> 00:02:17.471
Zann froze. The troll was changing as he watched it, its dull eyes growing brighter and its hands sparking with energy.

26
00:02:17.472 --> 00:02:20.726
"Uh-oh," thought Zann, guessing what that meant.

27
00:02:20.727 --> 00:02:25.070
Maybe the trolls hadn't been getting any extra energy from Morb for the past day or two.

28
00:02:25.071 --> 00:02:26.758
But they were getting it now.

29
00:02:26.759 --> 00:02:34.834
When he glanced at the rest of the trolls, who were starting to turn toward him, Zann saw that they were all charged with magical energy.

30
00:02:34.835 --> 00:02:39.850
"They're coming!" the old woman exclaimed. "Oh dear!"

31
00:02:39.851 --> 00:02:44.771
Zann didn't respond. He didn't have the heart to tell her that they were doomed.

32
00:02:44.772 --> 00:02:47.332
His friends were too far away to help.

33
00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.052
Even Zing couldn't possibly get to them in time.

34
00:02:50.053 --> 00:02:54.269
"Run, young man! Hurry!" The woman gave him a light shove.

35
00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:58.079
"You might be able to get away if they grab me first."

36
00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.936
Zann doubted that was true—the trolls were moving fast, thanks to their new infusion of magical energy.

37
00:03:03.937 --> 00:03:07.571
Even if it was true though, he couldn't abandon her.

38
00:03:07.572 --> 00:03:11.867
"It's okay," he said. "We'll figure something out together."

39
00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:15.819
But he knew it was hopeless. There was no escape this time.

40
00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.576
"Zann!" Teplo shouted, emerging from his hiding place.

41
00:03:19.577 --> 00:03:23.042
"Go!" Zann shouted. "Get out of here!"

42
00:03:23.043 --> 00:03:29.979
But Teplo hurried toward him. As he did, he yanked off his hat, revealing his wild red hair.

43
00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:37.704
"Yoo-hoo!" Teplo called out. "Look here, you dumb trolls! I've got a troll snack for you!"

44
00:03:37.705 --> 00:03:42.355
He snapped his fingers, conjuring up a giant blob of glowberry pudding.

45
00:03:42.356 --> 00:03:46.477
The trolls stopped and stared. A few started drooling immediately.

46
00:03:46.478 --> 00:03:55.664
"Yum!" Teplo exclaimed. He made a loud chewing sound as the illusion wavered and then quickly faded away.

47
00:03:55.665 --> 00:03:57.947
The trolls looked confused and annoyed.

48
00:03:57.948 --> 00:04:01.471
With howls of outrage, they all raced toward Teplo.

49
00:04:01.472 --> 00:04:08.751
He let out a whoop and ran away, heading deeper into the zoo, his bare ankles flashing beneath his too-short robe.

50
00:04:08.752 --> 00:04:12.973
Zann remained frozen, not understanding for a moment what was happening.

51
00:04:12.974 --> 00:04:17.179
Was Teplo crazy? He'd never be able to outrun the trolls!

52
00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:22.496
After expending all that energy, he probably couldn't even zap himself either!

53
00:04:22.497 --> 00:04:25.776
Then Teplo glanced back over his shoulder.

54
00:04:25.777 --> 00:04:31.538
"Go!" he shouted at Zann. "I'll say hi to your grandfather for you!"

55
00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:38.564
Zann realized that the old man was sacrificing his own freedom for Zann's. "No!" he cried.

56
00:04:38.565 --> 00:04:41.442
But it was too late to change what Teplo had done.

57
00:04:41.443 --> 00:04:44.987
Zann only hoped he could live up to Teplo's faith in him.

58
00:04:44.988 --> 00:04:52.262
"I think the trolls are distracted enough not to notice this," he said, grabbing the old woman's hand. "Zap!"

59
00:04:52.263 --> 00:04:58.643
They landed just outside the zoo. Others were still pouring through the hedge and running off in all directions.

60
00:04:58.644 --> 00:05:02.458
A young man let out a cry of relief and grabbed the old woman.

61
00:05:02.459 --> 00:05:06.569
Then Zann spotted Gliss and his other friends ahead in the crowd.

62
00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:11.299
Thrilled to see that Gliss was free, Zann sprinted after them.

63
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:15.167
Half an hour later, Zann finally had a chance to catch his breath.

64
00:05:15.168 --> 00:05:19.072
He and his friends were in an abandoned building a few blocks from the zoo.

65
00:05:19.073 --> 00:05:22.188
"This location should be safe," Fala said.

66
00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:26.072
"It's listed as vacant on all the official city records.

67
00:05:26.073 --> 00:05:29.522
Plus it has an old Shield spell still covering it."

68
00:05:29.523 --> 00:05:32.988
"Does that mean Morb can't find us here?" Darb asked.

69
00:05:32.989 --> 00:05:39.321
"I hope so," Fala replied. "Still, I'd better check the area for any sign of trolls.

70
00:05:39.322 --> 00:05:42.448
Don't use any magic while I'm gone."

71
00:05:42.449 --> 00:05:44.855
She hurried out, leaving the kids alone.

72
00:05:44.856 --> 00:05:51.231
"Wow!" Perda said. "That was crazy. What was it like being a prisoner, Gliss?"

73
00:05:51.232 --> 00:05:54.093
Gliss hadn't said much since being rescued.

74
00:05:54.094 --> 00:05:57.723
Now Zann noticed she looked distracted and agitated.

75
00:05:57.724 --> 00:06:03.697
"Are you okay?" Zann asked her. "Listen, I'm really sorry I—"

76
00:06:03.698 --> 00:06:09.507
Gliss didn't let him finish. "No, I'm not okay!" she exclaimed in a shaky voice.

77
00:06:09.508 --> 00:06:17.367
"You guys won't be either once you hear what I found out while I was a prisoner!"
